---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description =
  "The de-Google site doesn't spy on you. No Google Analytics, no cookies, no trackers — just anonymous, self-hosted page counts. Here's exactly what that means.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-20 pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-balance font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-[var(--color-brand-dark)] sm:text-4xl">
        {title}
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The whole point of this site is to help you claw back a little privacy. It would be
        pretty rich if the site itself spied on you. It doesn’t.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>No Google Analytics. Ever.</strong> I do count page views, using
          <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Plausible</a>,
          running on a server I own at <code>plausible.thompsonblack.us</code>. It sets no cookies,
          stores no IP addresses, doesn’t fingerprint you, and can’t follow you to other sites. It
          tells me a page got read — never who read it. That’s the whole extent of it.</li>
        <li><strong>No cookies.</strong> The site sets none, and neither does the analytics. Nothing
          is stored on your device, and nothing follows you around the web.</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party fonts or trackers.</strong> Fonts are self-hosted, so your browser
          never phones Google to render this page. The only request that leaves this site is that
          anonymous page count, and it goes to my own server — not an ad company. (It’s the de-Google
          site — anything else would be embarrassing.)</li>
        <li><strong>Search runs on your machine.</strong> The search box uses Pagefind: it loads a static index and runs entirely in your browser. Your search queries never leave your device.</li>
        <li><strong>No accounts, no forms, no email collection.</strong> There’s nothing here to sign up for, so there’s nothing for me to collect, sell, or lose.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The site is just static files served from a CDN. Like any website, the host that
        delivers those files can see standard request data (an IP address, roughly when a page
        was fetched) for the seconds it takes to serve the page — that’s how the internet
        works. I don’t touch it, store it, or use it to track or profile anyone. There is no
        database of you here, because there is no database of you anywhere on this site.
      </p>

      <p>If any of that ever changes, this page changes first.</p>

      <hr />

      <p>
        Questions? Find me at
        <a href="https://michalferber.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">michalferber.me</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
